# M&E scope fence

## Non-goals (STOP if prompt drifts here)

- Field data **collection** (KoboToolbox/ODK) — we ingest, not collect
- Dashboards / visualisation
- Full logframe / Theory of Change as a live system
- Real-time monitoring
- Multi-user approval workflows
- Level-3 open-ended agent autonomy
- Railway per-session sandboxes (use in-app job queue)
- Building Docling, Agent SDK, or Word engine from scratch
- n8n as orchestrator (plumbing only, post-launch for template ingestion)

## Forbidden core modifications

M&E must **not** modify:

| Core file / area | Why |
|------------------|-----|
| `app/services/export_service.py` | Proposal export stays python-docx |
| `app/services/proposal_service.py` | Pre-award product unchanged |
| `app/api/routes/proposals.py` | Proposal API unchanged |
| `app/ai/prompts/proposal.py` | Proposal prompts unchanged |
| Core models/migrations | No core table changes for M&E |

## M&E owns its export

Build `app/reports/services/report_export_service.py` using **docxtpl** + funder `.docx` templates under `app/reports/templates/docx/`.

## Reuse, don't fork

Import core auth, quota, profile, email, OpenAI client, humaniser patterns — extend via `app/reports/`, never patch core services.
